From a8f266daea19e3d6ea145b32161f12ab10b2beee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:08:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Install ripgrep for the database CI job

The db job added in #69 runs supabase/tests/run-local.sh, which checks
each race log with rg. The ubuntu-latest runner image does not ship
ripgrep, so the job failed after the expected VERSION_CONFLICT with
"rg: command not found". Install ripgrep in its own step, independent
of whether PostgreSQL 17 is already present on the runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0193fVPcTrjEFef6JTdVCFFj
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 26fd92c..a5626c8 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -36,6 +36,11 @@ jobs:
           node-version: 24
           cache: pnpm
       - run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+      - name: Install ripgrep; run-local.sh uses rg to inspect the race logs
+        run: |
+          sudo apt-get update
+          sudo apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ripgrep
+          rg --version
       - name: Install PostgreSQL 17 from the PGDG repository unless the runner image already has it
         run: |
           if [ ! -x "$PG_BIN/initdb" ]; then
